[1] 6252 - the shell’s job number and the PID of the background process.

getpid() - returns the PID of the process that calls it.

&var - gives the address of the variable var, which is a virtual address, not a physical one.

%p - the printf format specifier used to print a pointer address.

(void*) - casts the address to a generic pointer type, as %p expects.

fflush(stdout) - forces the output to be printed immediately instead of staying in the buffer, which matters when the output is not going straight to a terminal.

sleep(1) inside while(1) - keeps the process alive without using CPU so its address can be observed.

kill PID - stops a background process.
